ocities that you mentioned thank you  we will discuss at the  nato the foreign minister meeting today  and tomorrow tomorrow and the day after  tomorrow what more we can do  and i expect to be the the discussion  about how to provide further military  support what kind of systems how can we  enable the ukrainians  to stand up against invading russian  forces and the support we have already  provided  has an obvious impact we see  that they are able uh to actually take  out a lot of for instance ukrainian  sorry russian armor  and they have been able to actually  defeat them in several places and and  force them to totally change  their the russian war plan they're  moving out of kiev the north to regroup  and to move into the east  so yes i think we will consider what  more we can do  but at the same time  allies agree  that we should not send nato troops into  ukraine  and we should not send nato planes into  ukrainian airspace  and that's because we also have the  responsibility  to prevent  a war between russia and nato  that will cause more death more  destruction  and be even more dangerous  so yes we will  discuss  how we can further support  what more we can do to support ukraine  including what kind of  costs additional costs we can put on on  russia i welcome that allies are  discussing  more sanctions  but i don't expect any ally to be  uh in favor of uh  sending nato troops into ukraine  thank you very much this concludes this  press conference thank you
 

